  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building local capacity for conserving a recovering tiger population in the newly declared Amrabad Tiger Reserve, Telangana, India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to assist in the recovery of tiger numbers in the Eastern Ghats landscape, centered around the Amrabad Tiger Reserve (ATR), Nagarjunasagar Srisailam Tiger Reserve (NSTR) forest complex, such that these forests hold a thriving and viable tiger metapopulation. The project objectives are to rigorously document threats to tiger population recovery in terms of current prey base and human disturbance, build local capacity for tiger conservation and monitoring, and collaborate with the government in using data on tiger numbers and threat incidence to improve tiger conservation efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
